  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through next Monday)\nIssued at 1020 PM CDT Sun Sep 6 2026\n\nThe high remains in place on Wednesday, leading to another dry day \nand highs in the 90s for most of the area. We'll have to wait until \nThursday for a pattern change as troughing to the north suppresses \nthe high and sends a front south. Moisture will be streaming into \nthe area ahead of this front, and rain chances continue to trend \nup with each forecast package for Thursday and now range from \nabout 40 to 60 percent. Forecast soundings don't show much to be \nconcerned with right now with very poor lapse rates and shear less\nthan 30 knots. Low to medium rain chances will linger Friday and \ninto the weekend. As far as temperatures go, they'll cool some\nlate week, but will still be above normal.",
